  "code": "GL_INVENTORY_NEGATIVE_ASOF",
  "severity": "CRITICAL (AW engine)",
  "mechanism": "A late supplier invoice that lowers the material price after the material was consumed into FG produced the next day: the recost posts the FG part (and COGS part) of the delta dated on the material receipt day, before the FG lot existed, so the daily FG_INVENTORY balance is negative on that day (-1.50 / -1.57). The AW engine counts any negative daily inventory balance up to the close date as CRITICAL (supabase/dev/cp6_aw_t1_family.sql:386-399), so every later close is held. Cases whose receipt day was closed pass (the delta moves into the open period).",
  "example": "CALENDAR 1 month: receipt 23 Aug at estimated Rp10/unit, FG in 24 Aug (value 85), 2 pcs sold, invoice 23 Sep at Rp8.25: FG delta -1.57 and COGS delta -1.05 dated 23 Aug.",
  "options": [
   "(a) date the FG/COGS part of the recost on the affected FG or sale day (or the invoice processing day) - recost family change",
   "(b) the engine judges only the balance at the close date - loosens a check, owner permission required",
   "(c) keep HOLD"
  ],
  "decision": "owner/GPT; not changed by the writer"
 },
